# https://kb.isc.org/docs/isc-dhcp-44-manual-pages-dhcpd
# https://help.ubuntu.com/community/isc-dhcp-server

Installation: 
$ sudo apt-get install isc-dhcp-server 
--------------------------------------------
Configuration: 
$ sudo nano /etc/dhcp/dhpcd.conf

# Sample /etc/dhcpd.conf  --> from ubuntu.com 
# (add your comments here) 
default-lease-time 600;
max-lease-time 7200;
option subnet-mask 255.255.255.0;
option broadcast-address 192.168.1.255;
option routers 192.168.1.254;
option domain-name-servers 192.168.1.1, 192.168.1.2;
option domain-name "mydomain.example";

subnet 192.168.1.0 netmask 255.255.255.0 {
range 192.168.1.10 192.168.1.100;
range 192.168.1.150 192.168.1.200;
} 

For my vm set up to be able to download the isc-dhcp server it needed internet access and I wanted a closed network for the others - so the vm used two interfaces one on brigde and the other on internal
with the other 2 vms i put them on the same internal network 
can slod be predownloaded then change network setting in vm setting

To change Network Settings: 
$ sudo nano /etc/network/interfaces

Example of ours: 
-----------------------------------------
auto lo
iface lo inet loopback
auto eth1
iface eth1 inet manual

auto eth1 
iface eth1 inet static
    address 192.168.1.1
    netmask 255.255.255.0
------------------------------------------

Start and stop: 
$ sudo service isc-dhcp-server restart
$ sudo service isc-dhcp-server start
$ sudo service isc-dhcp-server stop 

-----------------------------------------------

To see leased addresssess:
$ dhcp-lease-list --lease /var/lib/dhcp/dhcpd.leases 

